{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>יכיר.</b> He shall make recognition of him, or he shall acknowledge before others who the firstborn is, if he is in a place where they do not know him. Or he is obligated from the outset to recognize who the firstborn among his sons is, if they are twins." "<b>לתת לו פי שנים.</b> That he take two portions: if there are three, they are reckoned as four, and he takes two portions. And if two sons, they are reckoned as three, and so for all. And in my opinion, this is also the meaning of ויהי גא פי שנים ברוחך אלי, as I explained in its place." "<b>כי הוא ראשית אונו.</b> The known, along with the upright, shall speak, and all Israel have the presumption of being upright."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "'ויהי גא' appears to be a citation in Aramaic/Arabic transliteration; left untranslated as in the original, as the referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:14.556073787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}